  "architecture_name": "[efficientnet_b0] efficientnet_b0_mixup_focal",
  "architecture_family": "efficientnet_b0",
  "description": "EfficientNet-B0 pretrained on ImageNet with 1\u21923 channel expansion, adaptive avg+max pooling concat, 512-unit dropout(0.3) hidden layer, and 206-unit sigmoid head, trained with focal loss and mixup augmentation to handle long-tail class imbalance.",
  "reasoning": "As the first experiment, EfficientNet-B0 offers the best quality-to-size tradeoff among the available pretrained backbones for spectrogram classification. It is small enough for CPU inference within 90 minutes on Kaggle, while ImageNet pretraining provides strong feature extraction even on single-channel mel-spectrograms. The concat of avg+max pooling captures both average energy and peak activations. Focal loss and mixup directly address the long-tail distribution challenge by up-weighting hard/rare examples and creating virtual training samples."
}
